If the gap stays bounded below as k grows, E_k is an expander family (a KLS-type dimension-free constant);
if it decays like 1/k or 1/3^k it is not.  The cycle-only column is the control (gap ~ 1/|U_k|^2).
log-log slope of the undirected gap vs |Z/3^k| over k >= 4: -0.224  (0 = expander, -1 = cycle-like in 1/N, -2 = pure cycle; -log_3 2 = -0.631 = halving per level)
successive gap ratios gap_k/gap_(k+1): ['2.0017', '1.9304', '1.5857', '1.3581', '1.2278', '1.1745', '1.1598']

